<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-lauschke-ex-vivo-scaling-mPSM> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Lauschke, Tsiairis, François & Aulehla (2013) scale-invariant phase-gradient encoding in ex vivo monolayer presomitic mesoderm (mPSM) (Mus musculus (mouse E10.5 tailbud LuVeLu Lfng-Venus monolayer presomitic mesoderm))" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/lauschke-ex-vivo-scaling-mPSM-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/lauschke-ex-vivo-scaling-mPSM-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/lauschke-ex-vivo-scaling-mPSM-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/lauschke-ex-vivo-scaling-mPSM-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/lauschke-ex-vivo-scaling-mPSM-5>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/lauschke-ex-vivo-scaling-mPSM-6> ;
    schema:about "Mus musculus (mouse E10.5 tailbud LuVeLu Lfng-Venus monolayer presomitic mesoderm)" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: Subcellular Lfng/Hes7 transcriptional-translational delay ODEs, explicit Notch-ligand delay-differential coupling, time-integrated morphogen transport on the moving boundary, 3D fibronectin traction mechanics, or cell movement/rearrangement within the reaggregate",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Bilateral dorsal somite row DoG peak and inter-somitic cleft segmentation on the vendored SEM (47.14 px mean spacing, CV = 0.2010; Panels E-F)",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Disordered reaggregate lattice of 1577 Kuramoto-Sakaguchi cells (K = 0.5 rad/min, eta = 0.25, a = 0.6 rad, correlation length 40 um): median 4 de novo pacemakers in cycles 1-3 consolidating to 1 in cycles 12-14 located 17.7 um from the local frequency maximum, local coherence 0.945; K = 0 -> coherence 0.004 and 0 sources, eta = 0 -> coherence 1.000 and 0 sources; K and eta sweeps (Panels H-I, reaggregate GIF)",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Quasi-static FGF/Wnt source-sink gradient (half-length exponent 1.000) vs fixed-length exponential gradient (exponent 0.000) driving dynamic wavelength relaxation d lambda/dt = -(lambda - c l_half)/tau_lambda with fixed-window segment gating: emergent alpha_8 = 0.1103 and mean Phi = 6.125 rad (2.5% from 2*pi) at tau_lambda = 35 min; alpha_8 = 0.5601 with tau_lambda = inf; constant 39.48 um segments (CV 0.032) with the fixed gradient (Panel G)",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Universal normalized phase-gradient collapse phi(r/R(t)) across R_0 in {150, 250, 350, 450} um (collapse std 9.93e-16 rad) vs non-scaling constant-gradient divergence; 2D circular mPSM LuVeLu target-wave kymograph; geometric radius progression with constant-velocity and DAPT (0 segments) controls (Panels A-D)",
        "reported_in_source: Aulehla et al. (2008) and Dubrulle & Pourquie (2004): graded posterior Wnt/beta-catenin and fgf8 signalling across the PSM, the latter set by mRNA decay (fixed length) rather than tissue size",
        "reported_in_source: Kuramoto (1984): a pacemaker with frequency excess beta k^2 in the nonlinear phase-diffusion equation emits a target wave of wavenumber k and the fastest pacemaker entrains the medium",
        "reported_in_source: Lauschke, Tsiairis, Francois & Aulehla (2013) Nature 493:101-105 scale-invariant phase-gradient encoding in ex vivo E10.5 mouse tailbud LuVeLu (Lfng-Venus) monolayer presomitic mesoderm (mPSM) with invariant ~2*pi phase span across the shrinking radius R(t), linear segment scaling S_n = alpha R(t_n) (alpha ~ 0.11) and wave velocity ~ R(t)/T_osc; Fig. 4 links the gradient steepening to a shrinking Wnt/FGF signalling domain",
        "reported_in_source: Tsiairis & Aulehla (2016) Cell 164:656-667: dissociated, randomised PSM cells re-synchronise LuVeLu oscillations in culture and self-organise multiple de novo target-wave foci",
        "transfer_boundary: Reaggregate pacemaker counts are compared with the paper's qualitative report of several foci (lower bound >= 2) and the Kuramoto single-dominant-pacemaker end state, not with digitised counts; the Sakaguchi lag a = 0.6 rad and kappa_init = 1 (partially synchronous initial phases) are modelling choices",
        "transfer_boundary: The FGF/Wnt gradient is quasi-static (analytic sinh / exponential profiles re-evaluated at each step), the sink-dominated limit is imposed through l_k = 1e6 um rather than derived from measured diffusion/decay constants, and c_lambda and delta_phi_seg are calibrated so that the adapted state reproduces Phi_0 = 2*pi and alpha = 0.11",
        "transfer_boundary: The vendored SEM specimen is a chick embryo (Wikimedia 'Aves Neural tube and somites in chick embryo', CC BY 4.0) used as a structural reference for somite periodicity; it is not mouse mPSM and no mPSM explant or reaggregate micrograph is compared" ;
