<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-lauschke-ex-vivo-scaling-mPSM-code-traceability> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Lauschke, Tsiairis, François & Aulehla (2013) scale-invariant phase-gradient encoding in ex vivo monolayer presomitic mesoderm (mPSM) — Code-to-model traceability: 92/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The module docstring maps Laws 1-6 to equations, source figures and Lean theorem names (L31-92); each Pass 3 function docstring states its equation and source (gradient L558-570, adaptation L618-624, lattice L851-858, detector L779-790); `morphoeval/math_kg_loops/lauschke-ex-vivo-scaling-mPSM.yaml` registers Laws 4-6 with lean_locus and code_locus. Deductions: Panel-level comments cite the Pass 3 mechanisms but not the Lauschke Fig. 4 sub-panel being reproduced (-3); the detector's threshold constants and the correlated-field construction are design choices without a literature anchor (-3); the kymograph's `_ = np.random.default_rng(seed)` is still a dead seed (-2)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "2014-lauschke-ex-vivo-scaling-mPSM.py L394–L394: Dead RNG in simulate_2d_mpsm_target_waves (seed has no effect) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2014-lauschke-ex-vivo-scaling-mPSM.py#L394-L394>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-lauschke-ex-vivo-scaling-mPSM-code-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-lauschke-ex-vivo-scaling-mPSM-code-traceability-2> ;
    pk1:hasScore 9.2e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-lauschke-ex-vivo-scaling-mPSM-model-fidelity> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Lauschke, Tsiairis, François & Aulehla (2013) scale-invariant phase-gradient encoding in ex vivo monolayer presomitic mesoderm (mPSM) — Model fidelity to source: 93/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Laws 1-3 are implemented as in Pass 2 (phi = omega_0 t - Phi_0 (r/R)^p, S_n = alpha R_n, R_{n+1} = (1-alpha) R_n, v = (2 pi/Phi_0) R/T_osc; L178-544). Pass 3 adds the mechanism the audit asked for: a quasi-static FGF/Wnt source-sink gradient W = W_0 sinh((R-r)/l_k)/sinh(R/l_k) with the fixed-length exponential alternative (L552-602), a wavelength relaxation ODE toward c_lambda l_half(t) with Phi(t) = 2 pi R/lambda and fixed-window gating S_n = R[1-(1-delta_phi_seg/Phi)^(1/p)] (L605-671), and a Kuramoto-Sakaguchi reaggregate lattice whose continuum limit is Kuramoto's nonlinear phase diffusion equation (L724-931), each with a machine-checked Lean statement (scale covariance, contraction, monotone dispersion). Deductions: c_lambda = (2 pi/Phi_0)/(1/2) and delta_phi_seg = Phi_0[1-(1-alpha)^p] are calibrated so that the adapted fixed point reproduces Phi_0 and alpha exactly, so the invariant is recovered rather than predicted (-3); the gradient is not time-integrated on the moving boundary and l_k = 1e6 um is a placeholder for the sink-dominated limit rather than measured FGF8/Wnt3a D and k (-2); the Sakaguchi lag a = 0.6 rad stands in for a Notch coupling delay without a delay-differential derivation (-2). Net 93 (-1 vs Pass 2: more mechanism, but the new constants are fitted to the law they are meant to explain)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "2014-lauschke-ex-vivo-scaling-mPSM.py L626–L627: c_lambda and delta_phi_seg are set from Phi_0 and alpha, so the adapted state reproduces the law by construction <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2014-lauschke-ex-vivo-scaling-mPSM.py#L626-L627>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-lauschke-ex-vivo-scaling-mPSM-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-lauschke-ex-vivo-scaling-mPSM-model-fidelity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-lauschke-ex-vivo-scaling-mPSM-model-fidelity-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-lauschke-ex-vivo-scaling-mPSM-model-fidelity-4> ;
    pk1:hasScore 9.3e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-lauschke-ex-vivo-scaling-mPSM-morphometric-validation> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Lauschke, Tsiairis, François & Aulehla (2013) scale-invariant phase-gradient encoding in ex vivo monolayer presomitic mesoderm (mPSM) — Morphometric validation: 90/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "`measure_morphoeval()` (L1012-1131) now returns 10 measurements with references and units: the five Pass 2 values (alpha 0.1100, Phi 6.2832 rad, S_1 38.5 um vs 38.9, Pearson r 0.9997, 47.14 px) plus the adaptive phase span 6.1253 rad vs 2*pi, emergent alpha_8 0.1103 vs 0.11, gradient half-length exponent 1.000 vs 1, early pacemaker count 4 vs the >= 2 lower bound and local coherence 0.9446 vs 1.0, each with the matching ablation in its note. Deductions: the two Tsiairis references are qualitative (a lower bound and a perfect-synchrony ceiling), not values digitised from the paper (-4); the 4-explant \"observed\" S_1 / S_5 / v_1 columns in the reference table have no figure or digitisation provenance, so the r = 0.9997 fit (carried from Pass 2) cannot be verified against Lauschke Fig. 3d (-4); the pacemaker count depends on the flux threshold 0.6 and rho = 30 um of the detector without a sensitivity check (-2)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "2014-lauschke-ex-vivo-scaling-mPSM.py L769–L835: Flow-source pacemaker detector: thresholds 0.6 and rho = 30 um fixed, no sensitivity sweep <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2014-lauschke-ex-vivo-scaling-mPSM.py#L769-L835>",
        "datasets/ex_vivo_scaling_mPSM/ex_vivo_scaling_mPSM_reference.json L145–L209: observed_S1_um / observed_S5_um / observed_v_wave_1_um_per_min lack a figure-digitisation source <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/datasets/ex_vivo_scaling_mPSM/ex_vivo_scaling_mPSM_reference.json#L145-L209>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-lauschke-ex-vivo-scaling-mPSM-measurement-de-novo-target-wave-pacemakers-in-the-disordered-reaggregate-lattice-median-of-cycles-1-3-cycles-12-14>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-lauschke-ex-vivo-scaling-mPSM-measurement-emergent-mpsm-total-phase-span-phi-t-under-fgf-wnt-driven-wavelength-adaptation-tau-lambda-t-osc-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-lauschke-ex-vivo-scaling-mPSM-measurement-emergent-proportional-scaling-ratio-alpha-s-8-r-t-8-at-cycle-8-under-wavelength-adaptation>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-lauschke-ex-vivo-scaling-mPSM-measurement-ex-vivo-mpsm-proportional-segment-scaling-slope-alpha-s-n-r-t-n>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-lauschke-ex-vivo-scaling-mPSM-measurement-fgf-wnt-signalling-gradient-half-length-scaling-exponent-d-ln-l-half-d-ln-r>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-lauschke-ex-vivo-scaling-mPSM-measurement-multi-size-mpsm-explant-segment-scaling-pearson-correlation-r>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-lauschke-ex-vivo-scaling-mPSM-measurement-reaggregate-local-notch-phase-coherence-cos-theta-j-theta-i-after-14-cycles>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-lauschke-ex-vivo-scaling-mPSM-measurement-standard-mpsm-explant-r-0-350-um-first-segment-width-s-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-lauschke-ex-vivo-scaling-mPSM-measurement-universal-normalized-phase-gradient-total-phase-span-delta-phi-total>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-lauschke-ex-vivo-scaling-mPSM-measurement-vertebrate-somite-psm-specimen-bilateral-somite-spacing-s-obs>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-lauschke-ex-vivo-scaling-mPSM-morphometric-validation-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-lauschke-ex-vivo-scaling-mPSM-morphometric-validation-2> ;
    pk1:hasScore 9e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-lauschke-ex-vivo-scaling-mPSM-overall> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Lauschke, Tsiairis, François & Aulehla (2013) scale-invariant phase-gradient encoding in ex vivo monolayer presomitic mesoderm (mPSM) — MorphoEval overall 89.9/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 3 remediation-round evaluation of `2014-lauschke-ex-vivo-scaling-mPSM.py` (89.9/100, down from 91.4 in Pass 2 because the round exposed and now prices defects that Pass 2 did not score). Both Pass 2 remediation items are closed: (1) an explicit FGF/Wnt source-sink signalling gradient whose half-length scales with R(t) (exponent 1.000 vs 0.000 for a Dubrulle-Pourquie fixed-length decay gradient) drives a dynamic wavelength relaxation d lambda/dt = -(lambda - c l_half)/tau_lambda with fixed-window segment gating, so alpha = S_n/R(t_n) is now an output: 0.1103 at cycle 8 and mean Phi = 6.125 rad (2.5% from 2*pi) for tau_lambda = T_osc/4, drifting to alpha_8 = 0.5601 when adaptation is frozen and to constant 39.5 um segments with the fixed-length gradient (Panel G, tau_lambda sweep); (2) a Tsiairis & Aulehla (2016) disordered reaggregate lattice of 1577 Kuramoto-Sakaguchi cells with spatially correlated frequency heterogeneity in which phase-gradient flow-source detection finds median 4 de novo target-wave pacemakers in cycles 1-3 consolidating to 1 (17.7 um from the local frequency maximum) by cycles 12-14, with K = 0 and eta = 0 ablations giving 0 pacemakers and K / eta sweeps (Panels H-I, new reaggregate GIF). Six machine- checked Lean 4 theorems (3 new, 0 sorrys), 10 reference-anchored measurements (5 new) and 18 new self-test assertions back the additions. Remaining defects: the vendored \"mouse\" specimen is a chick SEM, the calibration of c_lambda and delta_phi_seg partly builds the invariant back in, the gradient is quasi-static with a placeholder l_k, fully random initial phases pin spiral defects, the 4-explant \"observed\" columns lack digitisation provenance and the --R0/--alpha/--T-osc/--seed flags do not reach the default render. Overall 89.9/100 (faithfulness 89.5, reproducibility 90.9); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit d58a084; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 93, Morphological realism / specimen match 85, Parameter expressivity 93, Morphometric validation 90, Source and data traceability 91, Code-to-model traceability 92, Reproducibility package 90. Output judged: docs/media/ex_vivo_scaling_mPSM_comparison.png: rendered output of 2014-lauschke-ex-vivo-scaling-mPSM.py at d58a084, image/png, 2083380 B, 2775×2475 px, artifact_sha256 7d82231491cf8c8a7e9f6d71c63fe402e0de3485aa001f798cf6dca97220276d (sha256 7d82231491cf8c8a7e9f6d71c63fe402e0de3485aa001f798cf6dca97220276d), spec_fingerprint db42a42f7fc47de46b4f32f0f0564c2111d321e4401a2d84074e25a13a453b30. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: db42a42f7fc47de46b4f32f0f0564c2111d321e4401a2d84074e25a13a453b30; artifact_sha256: 7d82231491cf8c8a7e9f6d71c63fe402e0de3485aa001f798cf6dca97220276d; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/ex_vivo_scaling_mPSM/ex_vivo_scaling_mPSM_reference.json=faa9b63279e4f169..., datasets/ex_vivo_scaling_mPSM/mouse_mpsm_somites_specimen.jpg=8b80971796cb29e2..., datasets/ex_vivo_scaling_mPSM/scout_manifest.json=ed97fcae27d8072b...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-ex-vivo-scaling-mPSM-audit-v2. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Lauschke, Tsiairis, Francois & Aulehla (2013) Nature 493:101-105 scale-invariant phase-gradient encoding in ex vivo E10.5 mouse tailbud LuVeLu (Lfng-Venus) monolayer presomitic mesoderm (mPSM) with invariant ~2*pi phase span across the shrinking radius R(t), linear segment scaling S_n = alpha R(t_n) (alpha ~ 0.11) and wave velocity ~ R(t)/T_osc; Fig. 4 links the gradient steepening to a shrinking Wnt/FGF signalling domain | Aulehla et al. (2008) and Dubrulle & Pourquie (2004): graded posterior Wnt/beta-catenin and fgf8 signalling across the PSM, the latter set by mRNA decay (fixed length) rather than tissue size | Tsiairis & Aulehla (2016) Cell 164:656-667: dissociated, randomised PSM cells re-synchronise LuVeLu oscillations in culture and self-organise multiple de novo target-wave foci | Kuramoto (1984): a pacemaker with frequency excess beta k^2 in the nonlinear phase-diffusion equation emits a target wave of wavenumber k and the fastest pacemaker entrains the medium; reconstructed_in_script: Universal normalized phase-gradient collapse phi(r/R(t)) across R_0 in {150, 250, 350, 450} um (collapse std 9.93e-16 rad) vs non-scaling constant-gradient divergence; 2D circular mPSM LuVeLu target-wave kymograph; geometric radius progression with constant-velocity and DAPT (0 segments) controls (Panels A-D) | Quasi-static FGF/Wnt source-sink gradient (half-length exponent 1.000) vs fixed-length exponential gradient (exponent 0.000) driving dynamic wavelength relaxation d lambda/dt = -(lambda - c l_half)/tau_lambda with fixed-window segment gating: emergent alpha_8 = 0.1103 and mean Phi = 6.125 rad (2.5% from 2*pi) at tau_lambda = 35 min; alpha_8 = 0.5601 with tau_lambda = inf; constant 39.48 um segments (CV 0.032) with the fixed gradient (Panel G) | Disordered reaggregate lattice of 1577 Kuramoto-Sakaguchi cells (K = 0.5 rad/min, eta = 0.25, a = 0.6 rad, correlation length 40 um): median 4 de novo pacemakers in cycles 1-3 consolidating to 1 in cycles 12-14 located 17.7 um from the local frequency maximum, local coherence 0.945; K = 0 -> coherence 0.004 and 0 sources, eta = 0 -> coherence 1.000 and 0 sources; K and eta sweeps (Panels H-I, reaggregate GIF) | Bilateral dorsal somite row DoG peak and inter-somitic cleft segmentation on the vendored SEM (47.14 px mean spacing, CV = 0.2010; Panels E-F); transfer_boundary: The vendored SEM specimen is a chick embryo (Wikimedia 'Aves Neural tube and somites in chick embryo', CC BY 4.0) used as a structural reference for somite periodicity; it is not mouse mPSM and no mPSM explant or reaggregate micrograph is compared | The FGF/Wnt gradient is quasi-static (analytic sinh / exponential profiles re-evaluated at each step), the sink-dominated limit is imposed through l_k = 1e6 um rather than derived from measured diffusion/decay constants, and c_lambda and delta_phi_seg are calibrated so that the adapted state reproduces Phi_0 = 2*pi and alpha = 0.11 | Reaggregate pacemaker counts are compared with the paper's qualitative report of several foci (lower bound >= 2) and the Kuramoto single-dominant-pacemaker end state, not with digitised counts; the Sakaguchi lag a = 0.6 rad and kappa_init = 1 (partially synchronous initial phases) are modelling choices; does_not_claim: Subcellular Lfng/Hes7 transcriptional-translational delay ODEs, explicit Notch-ligand delay-differential coupling, time-integrated morphogen transport on the moving boundary, 3D fibronectin traction mechanics, or cell movement/rearrangement within the reaggregate." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: 2014-lauschke-ex-vivo-scaling-mPSM.py:1806-1826 and 394 — --R0/--alpha/--T-osc/--seed do not reach the default render and the kymograph RNG is dead. Forward CLI parameters to render_comparison_figure / render_growth_gif / render_reaggregate_gif (or remove the flags), and add a requirements lock for the slot.",
        "remediation needed: 2014-lauschke-ex-vivo-scaling-mPSM.py:552-602 and reference.json `fgf_wnt_signaling_gradient` — the gradient is quasi-static with l_k = 1e6 um as a placeholder. Time-integrate dW/dt = D W'' - k W on the moving boundary with measured FGF8/Wnt3a D and k and a boundary sink, and report the actual d ln l_half / d ln R exponent instead of the imposed limit.",
        "remediation needed: 2014-lauschke-ex-vivo-scaling-mPSM.py:626-627 and 605-671 — c_lambda = (2 pi/Phi_0)/(1/2) and delta_phi_seg = Phi_0[1-(1-alpha)^p] are calibrated from the very invariants the adaptation is meant to explain. Replace the relaxation ODE by a coupled Notch phase-oscillator continuum on [0, R(t)] whose local frequency omega(W(r,t)) is a published Wnt/FGF-dependent function (Tsiairis & Aulehla 2016 Fig. 6), so that Phi(t) -> 2 pi and alpha emerge from omega(W) and the coupling without c_lambda.",
        "remediation needed: 2014-lauschke-ex-vivo-scaling-mPSM.py:769-835 and 916-931 — the pacemaker detector uses fixed flux_threshold = 0.6 and rho = 30 um, and the K / eta sweeps use a single seed. Add a threshold sensitivity sweep and seed-averaged (>= 5 seeds) pacemaker counts with confidence intervals.",
        "remediation needed: 2014-lauschke-ex-vivo-scaling-mPSM.py:865 and 132 — kappa_init = 1 (partially synchronous initial phases) is required for target waves; kappa_init = 0 pins spiral defects (0 sources, coherence 0.91). Add a defect-annihilation mechanism (longer-range coupling, delayed onset of oscillations, or cell motility) so fully random initial phases re-synchronise as in Tsiairis & Aulehla (2016), and report the topological defect count as a measurement.",
        "remediation needed: datasets/ex_vivo_scaling_mPSM/ex_vivo_scaling_mPSM_reference.json:145-209 — observed_S1_um / observed_S5_um / observed_v_wave_1_um_per_min carry no figure-digitisation provenance. Digitise Lauschke 2013 Fig. 3d (segment size vs mPSM size) and Fig. 4 velocity data, record the digitisation method, and recompute the Pearson r / RMSE measurements against those points.",
        "remediation needed: datasets/ex_vivo_scaling_mPSM/mouse_mpsm_somites_specimen.jpg and reference.json:41-45 — the file is a chick embryo SEM named as mouse. Keep the SHA-pinned file but add a correctly named alias/metadata entry stating Gallus gallus, and vendor a CC-licensed mouse mPSM explant or reaggregate micrograph (or digitise Lauschke 2013 Fig. 1 / Tsiairis 2016 Fig. 2 outlines) so Panels B, G, H have an image comparison." ;
    pk1:hasScore 8.99e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-lauschke-ex-vivo-scaling-mPSM-parameter-expressivity> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Lauschke, Tsiairis, François & Aulehla (2013) scale-invariant phase-gradient encoding in ex vivo monolayer presomitic mesoderm (mPSM) — Parameter expressivity: 93/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The 4-explant series (R_0 150-450 um), constant-velocity and DAPT controls remain (L458-544); Pass 3 adds a tau_lambda sweep {5, 35, 70, 280, inf} min whose phase-span error grows monotonically (0.3%, 2.5%, 5.0%, 17.6%, 38.8%) with emergent alpha_8 0.110 -> 0.560, the fixed-length-gradient control, and K {0, 0.25, 0.5, 1} and eta {0, 0.1, 0.25, 0.4} sweeps of the reaggregate (coherence 0.00 -> 0.98 with K; 0 foci at eta = 0, 4 -> 1 at eta >= 0.1), each visible in Panels G and I and exposed through --tau-lambda, --gradient-mode, --K, --eta, --kappa-init. Deductions: the sweeps are reported as text in Panel I rather than rendered pullbacks (-3); the K/eta sweep snapshots use a single seed so the monotonic claims are not seed-averaged (-2); --R0/--alpha/--T-osc/--seed only act under --print-variant (-2)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
