<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/lauschke-ex-vivo-scaling-mPSM-1> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Lauschke et al. (2013) Proportional Segment Scaling Law under Invariant Phase Span" ;
    dct:description "Establishes linear scale-invariance of embryonic segment size with residual tissue radius via a constant 2*pi total phase span across the active mPSM | Variables: S_n: newly specified concentric segment width at cycle n (um); R(t_n): residual unsegmented mPSM radius (um); alpha: dimensionless proportional scaling slope (0.11)" ;
    dct:source "Lauschke, Tsiairis, Francois & Aulehla (2013) Nature 493(7430):101-105 Figs. 2-4" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2014-lauschke-ex-vivo-scaling-mPSM.py#L178-L269>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_026_ex_vivo_scaling_mPSM.lean#L22-L44> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def scaled_segment_width (alpha R : Nat) : Nat :=
  alpha * R
theorem lauschke_2013_proportional_segment_scaling (alpha k R R1 R2 : Nat) :
    scaled_segment_width alpha (k * R) = k * scaled_segment_width alpha R ∧
    scaled_segment_width alpha (R1 + R2) =
      scaled_segment_width alpha R1 + scaled_segment_width alpha R2"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "S_n = alpha * R(t_n),  where Delta_phi_total = phi(0, t) - phi(R(t), t) = Phi_0 = 2*pi" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-642-69689-3>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cell.2016.01.028>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature02216>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature11804>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/ncb1679>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1088/1478-3975/13/3/036009> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Scale-Invariant Kinematic Phase-Gradient Encoding (Ex Vivo Monolayer PSM)" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_026.scaled_segment_width" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_026.lauschke_2013_proportional_segment_scaling" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/lauschke-ex-vivo-scaling-mPSM-2> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Lauschke et al. (2013) Geometric Residual mPSM Radius Progression & Conservation Law" ;
    dct:description "Governs the inward periphery-to-center geometric contraction of the active mPSM domain and exact radial conservation across successive segmentation cycles | Variables: R_n: residual mPSM radius at cycle n (um); R_0: initial mPSM explant radius (um); S_n: n-th concentric segment width (um)" ;
    dct:source "Lauschke, Tsiairis, Francois & Aulehla (2013) Nature 493(7430):101-105 Figs. 1-3" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2014-lauschke-ex-vivo-scaling-mPSM.py#L275-L372>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_026_ex_vivo_scaling_mPSM.lean#L46-L67> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def residual_mpsm_radius_step (M alpha R_n : Int) : Int :=
  (M - alpha) * R_n
def budded_segment_step (alpha R_n : Int) : Int :=
  alpha * R_n
theorem lauschke_2013_geometric_residual_radius_conservation (M alpha R_n : Int) :
    residual_mpsm_radius_step M alpha R_n + budded_segment_step alpha R_n = M * R_n"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "R(t_{n+1}) = R(t_n) - S_n = (1 - alpha) * R(t_n) = R_0 * (1 - alpha)^n" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-642-69689-3>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cell.2016.01.028>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature02216>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature11804>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/ncb1679>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1088/1478-3975/13/3/036009> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Scale-Invariant Kinematic Phase-Gradient Encoding (Ex Vivo Monolayer PSM)" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_026.residual_mpsm_radius_step" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_026.lauschke_2013_geometric_residual_radius_conservation" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/lauschke-ex-vivo-scaling-mPSM-3> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Lauschke et al. (2013) Radial Notch Phase-Wave Velocity Scaling Law" ;
    dct:description "Explains why LuVeLu Notch oscillation waves propagate faster in larger mPSM explants and decelerate as R(t) shrinks while maintaining a 2*pi phase span | Variables: v_wave(t): radial LuVeLu Notch phase-wave propagation speed (um/min); lambda(t): effective radial phase wavelength (um); T_osc: central pacemaker clock period (140 min)" ;
    dct:source "Lauschke, Tsiairis, Francois & Aulehla (2013) Nature 493(7430):101-105 Fig. 4" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2014-lauschke-ex-vivo-scaling-mPSM.py#L378-L544>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_026_ex_vivo_scaling_mPSM.lean#L69-L90> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def phase_wave_kinematic_residual (v_wave T_osc lambda_ratio R : Int) : Int :=
  v_wave * T_osc - lambda_ratio * R
theorem lauschke_2013_phase_wave_velocity_scaling (lambda_ratio T_osc c : Int) :
    phase_wave_kinematic_residual (lambda_ratio * c) T_osc lambda_ratio (T_osc * c) = 0"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "v_wave(t) = lambda(t) / T_osc = (2*pi / Phi_0) * (R(t) / T_osc)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-642-69689-3>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cell.2016.01.028>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature02216>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature11804>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/ncb1679>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1088/1478-3975/13/3/036009> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Scale-Invariant Kinematic Phase-Gradient Encoding (Ex Vivo Monolayer PSM)" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_026.phase_wave_kinematic_residual" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_026.lauschke_2013_phase_wave_velocity_scaling" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/lauschke-ex-vivo-scaling-mPSM-4> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "FGF/Wnt Source-Sink Signalling Gradient Scale Covariance (shrinking gradient on the active mPSM)" ;
    dct:description "Supplies the shrinking FGF/Wnt gradient of Lauschke et al. (2013) Fig. 4 whose length scales with the residual mPSM radius and drives wavelength adaptation; the fixed-length exponential gradient (Dubrulle & Pourquie 2004) is the mechanistic non-scaling control | Variables: W(r,t): FGF/Wnt signalling level (W_0 at the central source, 0 at the peripheral determination-front sink); l_k = sqrt(D/k): diffusion-decay length (um); l_half: half-maximum length of the gradient (um)" ;
    dct:source "Lauschke, Tsiairis, Francois & Aulehla (2013) Nature 493(7430):101-105 Fig. 4; Aulehla et al. (2008) Nat Cell Biol 10:186-193; Dubrulle & Pourquie (2004) Nature 427:419-422" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2014-lauschke-ex-vivo-scaling-mPSM.py#L552-L602>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_026_ex_vivo_scaling_mPSM.lean#L100-L118> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def source_sink_gradient (W0 R r : Int) : Int :=
  W0 * (R - r)
theorem lauschke_2013_fgf_wnt_gradient_scale_covariance (W0 k R r : Int) :
    source_sink_gradient W0 (k * R) (k * r) = k * source_sink_gradient W0 R r"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "D W'' - k W = 0, W(0) = W_0, W(R) = 0  =>  W = W_0 sinh((R - r)/l_k)/sinh(R/l_k);  l_k >> R: W = W_0 (1 - r/R), l_half = R/2;  W(k R, k r) = k W(R, r) (scaled units)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-642-69689-3>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cell.2016.01.028>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature02216>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature11804>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/ncb1679>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1088/1478-3975/13/3/036009> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Scale-Invariant Kinematic Phase-Gradient Encoding (Ex Vivo Monolayer PSM)" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_026.source_sink_gradient" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_026.lauschke_2013_fgf_wnt_gradient_scale_covariance" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/lauschke-ex-vivo-scaling-mPSM-5> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Dynamic Notch Phase-Wave Wavelength Adaptation to the FGF/Wnt Gradient Length" ;
    dct:description "Closes the Pass 2 remediation item: the 2*pi phase span and alpha = 0.11 are recovered dynamically from the shrinking FGF/Wnt gradient (mean Phi = 6.125 rad, alpha_8 = 0.1103 at tau_lambda = T_osc/4) and lost when adaptation is frozen (alpha_8 = 0.560) or the gradient has fixed length (constant 39.5 um segments) | Variables: lambda(t): Notch phase-wave wavelength (um); tau_lambda: adaptation time (35 min default, inf = frozen ablation); Phi(t): dynamic total phase span (rad); delta_phi_seg: peripheral gating window (0.9144 rad); alpha = S_n/R(t_n): emergent scaling ratio" ;
    dct:source "Lauschke, Tsiairis, Francois & Aulehla (2013) Nature 493(7430):101-105 Fig. 4; Beaupeux & Francois (2016) Phys Biol 13:036009" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2014-lauschke-ex-vivo-scaling-mPSM.py#L605-L717>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_026_ex_vivo_scaling_mPSM.lean#L120-L144> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def wavelength_adaptation_error_step (M h e : Int) : Int :=
  (M - h) * e
theorem lauschke_2013_wavelength_adaptation_contraction (M h e : Int)
    (h0 : 0 ≤ h) (hM : h ≤ M) :
    Int.natAbs (wavelength_adaptation_error_step M h e) ≤ Int.natAbs (M * e)"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "d lambda/dt = -(lambda - c_lambda l_half(t))/tau_lambda;  Phi(t) = 2 pi R(t)/lambda(t);  phi(r,t) = omega_0 t - Phi(t) (r/R(t))^p;  S_n = R(t_n)[1 - (1 - delta_phi_seg/Phi(t_n))^(1/p)], delta_phi_seg = Phi_0[1 - (1 - alpha)^p];  discrete error step M e_{n+1} = (M - h) e_n" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-642-69689-3>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cell.2016.01.028>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature02216>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature11804>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/ncb1679>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1088/1478-3975/13/3/036009> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Scale-Invariant Kinematic Phase-Gradient Encoding (Ex Vivo Monolayer PSM)" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_026.wavelength_adaptation_error_step" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_026.lauschke_2013_wavelength_adaptation_contraction" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/lauschke-ex-vivo-scaling-mPSM-6> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Kuramoto-Sakaguchi Reaggregate Lattice & Target-Wave Pacemaker Dispersion (Tsiairis & Aulehla 2016)" ;
    dct:description "Closes the Pass 2 remediation item: 1577 cells on a jittered hexagonal disc self-organise median 4 de novo target-wave pacemakers (cycles 1-3) that consolidate to 1 at the local frequency maximum (cycles 12-14); K = 0 stays incoherent, eta = 0 synchronises with no pacemaker | Variables: theta_i: LuVeLu phase of cell i; omega_i: intrinsic frequency (omega_0 = 2 pi / 140 min, relative heterogeneity eta = 0.25, correlation length 40 um); K: Notch coupling (0.5 rad/min); a: Sakaguchi phase lag (0.6 rad); beta k^2: frequency excess of a pacemaker emitting wavenumber k" ;
    dct:source "Tsiairis & Aulehla (2016) Cell 164(4):656-667 Figs. 2-4; Kuramoto (1984) Chemical Oscillations, Waves, and Turbulence, Springer, Ch. 5-6" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2014-lauschke-ex-vivo-scaling-mPSM.py#L724-L931>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_026_ex_vivo_scaling_mPSM.lean#L146-L166> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def target_wave_frequency_excess (beta k : Nat) : Nat :=
  beta * k * k
theorem tsiairis_2016_pacemaker_dispersion_monotone (beta k1 k2 : Nat) (h : k1 ≤ k2) :
    target_wave_frequency_excess beta k1 ≤ target_wave_frequency_excess beta k2"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "d theta_i/dt = omega_i + (K/n_i) sum_j [sin(theta_j - theta_i - a) + sin a], omega_i = omega_0 (1 + eta xi_i);  continuum: theta_t = omega + D lap theta + beta |grad theta|^2, D = K cos(a) d^2/4, beta = K sin(a) d^2/4;  pacemaker excess Delta omega = beta k^2 (monotone in k)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-642-69689-3>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cell.2016.01.028>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature02216>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature11804>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/ncb1679>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1088/1478-3975/13/3/036009> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Scale-Invariant Kinematic Phase-Gradient Encoding (Ex Vivo Monolayer PSM)" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_026.target_wave_frequency_excess" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_026.tsiairis_2016_pacemaker_dispersion_monotone" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/lauschke-ex-vivo-scaling-mPSM-1> a skos:Concept,
        pk1:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Lauschke et al. (2013) Proportional Segment Scaling Law under Invariant Phase Span" ;
    dct:description "Establishes linear scale-invariance of embryonic segment size with residual tissue radius via a constant 2*pi total phase span across the active mPSM | Variables: S_n: newly specified concentric segment width at cycle n (um); R(t_n): residual unsegmented mPSM radius (um); alpha: dimensionless proportional scaling slope (0.11)" ;
    dct:source "Lauschke, Tsiairis, Francois & Aulehla (2013) Nature 493(7430):101-105 Figs. 2-4" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2014-lauschke-ex-vivo-scaling-mPSM.py#L178-L269>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_026_ex_vivo_scaling_mPSM.lean#L22-L44> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def scaled_segment_width (alpha R : Nat) : Nat :=
  alpha * R
theorem lauschke_2013_proportional_segment_scaling (alpha k R R1 R2 : Nat) :
    scaled_segment_width alpha (k * R) = k * scaled_segment_width alpha R ∧
    scaled_segment_width alpha (R1 + R2) =
      scaled_segment_width alpha R1 + scaled_segment_width alpha R2"""^^pk1:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "S_n = alpha * R(t_n),  where Delta_phi_total = phi(0, t) - phi(R(t), t) = Phi_0 = 2*pi" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-642-69689-3>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cell.2016.01.028>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature02216>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature11804>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/ncb1679>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1088/1478-3975/13/3/036009> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk1:hypothesisType "Scale-Invariant Kinematic Phase-Gradient Encoding (Ex Vivo Monolayer PSM)" ;
    pk1:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_026.scaled_segment_width" ;
    pk1:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_026.lauschke_2013_proportional_segment_scaling" ;
    pk1:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/lauschke-ex-vivo-scaling-mPSM-2> a skos:Concept,
        pk1:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Lauschke et al. (2013) Geometric Residual mPSM Radius Progression & Conservation Law" ;
    dct:description "Governs the inward periphery-to-center geometric contraction of the active mPSM domain and exact radial conservation across successive segmentation cycles | Variables: R_n: residual mPSM radius at cycle n (um); R_0: initial mPSM explant radius (um); S_n: n-th concentric segment width (um)" ;
    dct:source "Lauschke, Tsiairis, Francois & Aulehla (2013) Nature 493(7430):101-105 Figs. 1-3" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2014-lauschke-ex-vivo-scaling-mPSM.py#L275-L372>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_026_ex_vivo_scaling_mPSM.lean#L46-L67> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def residual_mpsm_radius_step (M alpha R_n : Int) : Int :=
  (M - alpha) * R_n
def budded_segment_step (alpha R_n : Int) : Int :=
  alpha * R_n
theorem lauschke_2013_geometric_residual_radius_conservation (M alpha R_n : Int) :
    residual_mpsm_radius_step M alpha R_n + budded_segment_step alpha R_n = M * R_n"""^^pk1:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "R(t_{n+1}) = R(t_n) - S_n = (1 - alpha) * R(t_n) = R_0 * (1 - alpha)^n" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-642-69689-3>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cell.2016.01.028>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature02216>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature11804>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/ncb1679>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1088/1478-3975/13/3/036009> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk1:hypothesisType "Scale-Invariant Kinematic Phase-Gradient Encoding (Ex Vivo Monolayer PSM)" ;
    pk1:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_026.residual_mpsm_radius_step" ;
    pk1:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_026.lauschke_2013_geometric_residual_radius_conservation" ;
    pk1:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/lauschke-ex-vivo-scaling-mPSM-3> a skos:Concept,
        pk1:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Lauschke et al. (2013) Radial Notch Phase-Wave Velocity Scaling Law" ;
    dct:description "Explains why LuVeLu Notch oscillation waves propagate faster in larger mPSM explants and decelerate as R(t) shrinks while maintaining a 2*pi phase span | Variables: v_wave(t): radial LuVeLu Notch phase-wave propagation speed (um/min); lambda(t): effective radial phase wavelength (um); T_osc: central pacemaker clock period (140 min)" ;
    dct:source "Lauschke, Tsiairis, Francois & Aulehla (2013) Nature 493(7430):101-105 Fig. 4" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2014-lauschke-ex-vivo-scaling-mPSM.py#L378-L544>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_026_ex_vivo_scaling_mPSM.lean#L69-L90> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def phase_wave_kinematic_residual (v_wave T_osc lambda_ratio R : Int) : Int :=
  v_wave * T_osc - lambda_ratio * R
theorem lauschke_2013_phase_wave_velocity_scaling (lambda_ratio T_osc c : Int) :
    phase_wave_kinematic_residual (lambda_ratio * c) T_osc lambda_ratio (T_osc * c) = 0"""^^pk1:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "v_wave(t) = lambda(t) / T_osc = (2*pi / Phi_0) * (R(t) / T_osc)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-642-69689-3>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cell.2016.01.028>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature02216>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature11804>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/ncb1679>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1088/1478-3975/13/3/036009> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk1:hypothesisType "Scale-Invariant Kinematic Phase-Gradient Encoding (Ex Vivo Monolayer PSM)" ;
    pk1:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_026.phase_wave_kinematic_residual" ;
    pk1:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_026.lauschke_2013_phase_wave_velocity_scaling" ;
    pk1:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/lauschke-ex-vivo-scaling-mPSM-4> a skos:Concept,
        pk1:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "FGF/Wnt Source-Sink Signalling Gradient Scale Covariance (shrinking gradient on the active mPSM)" ;
    dct:description "Supplies the shrinking FGF/Wnt gradient of Lauschke et al. (2013) Fig. 4 whose length scales with the residual mPSM radius and drives wavelength adaptation; the fixed-length exponential gradient (Dubrulle & Pourquie 2004) is the mechanistic non-scaling control | Variables: W(r,t): FGF/Wnt signalling level (W_0 at the central source, 0 at the peripheral determination-front sink); l_k = sqrt(D/k): diffusion-decay length (um); l_half: half-maximum length of the gradient (um)" ;
    dct:source "Lauschke, Tsiairis, Francois & Aulehla (2013) Nature 493(7430):101-105 Fig. 4; Aulehla et al. (2008) Nat Cell Biol 10:186-193; Dubrulle & Pourquie (2004) Nature 427:419-422" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2014-lauschke-ex-vivo-scaling-mPSM.py#L552-L602>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_026_ex_vivo_scaling_mPSM.lean#L100-L118> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def source_sink_gradient (W0 R r : Int) : Int :=
  W0 * (R - r)
theorem lauschke_2013_fgf_wnt_gradient_scale_covariance (W0 k R r : Int) :
    source_sink_gradient W0 (k * R) (k * r) = k * source_sink_gradient W0 R r"""^^pk1:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "D W'' - k W = 0, W(0) = W_0, W(R) = 0  =>  W = W_0 sinh((R - r)/l_k)/sinh(R/l_k);  l_k >> R: W = W_0 (1 - r/R), l_half = R/2;  W(k R, k r) = k W(R, r) (scaled units)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-642-69689-3>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cell.2016.01.028>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature02216>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature11804>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/ncb1679>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1088/1478-3975/13/3/036009> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk1:hypothesisType "Scale-Invariant Kinematic Phase-Gradient Encoding (Ex Vivo Monolayer PSM)" ;
    pk1:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_026.source_sink_gradient" ;
    pk1:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_026.lauschke_2013_fgf_wnt_gradient_scale_covariance" ;
    pk1:leanVerified true .

